title: P09 Step 1 - why the reservation id moved into the database (observed on PostgreSQL 16 and SQLite)
---
sequenceDiagram
  autonumber
  participant M as Maya's transaction
  participant DB as Database
  participant O as Omar's transaction

  rect rgb(255, 235, 238)
  Note over M,O: Version 5: id = 'R' || (101 + count(*))
  M->>DB: count(*) -> 0, INSERT R101 (not committed yet)
  O->>DB: count(*) -> 0 (R101 is invisible) - INSERT R101
  Note over O,DB: Omar's INSERT waits for Maya's transaction, then the primary key<br/>refuses it
  DB--xO: 23505 duplicate key reservations_pkey - the app answered 500 InternalError (P07)
  end

  rect rgb(232, 245, 233)
  Note over M,O: Version 6: next_reservation_id() asks the database
  M->>DB: nextval('reservation_ids') -> 101 (PostgreSQL, SQLite: UPDATE reservation_ids RETURNING)
  O->>DB: nextval -> 102 - no wait, never the same number
  M->>DB: ROLLBACK
  O->>DB: nextval -> 103 - 101 is not handed out again (a gap, never a duplicate)
  end
